I've written a plan with two tasks and committed it as 2ead717c. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so I force-added the files, the same way the assessment commit just before it was added.

Task 1 — Part of #1184 (product, security). The problem: a deny list written over several lines under [permissions] or [directories] sets up no deny rule. doctor warns about it, but the rule isn't in force. The assessment confirmed this on the built binary, and Python's TOML reader (tomllib) reads the same file correctly. The task:
• moves both parsers onto the TOML table that's already parsed, covering every way of writing the list (one line, several lines, comments, dotted keys, inline tables, spaces in the header);
• removes the "could not read" warning for shapes that now read, rather than teaching the old line reader new shapes;
• starts by listing everything that reads those two sections;
• tracks the ticket's own done-when measure, the number of line-by-line reading entry points. The task requires that number to go down.

It includes a deliberate sabotage check (break the new read, watch the tests fail by name, restore in the same command). Results go on the ticket as they come in. Writing config back without losing comments, and deleting the hand parser, stay open on #1184.

Task 2 — Fixes #1196 (product, closes a backlog issue). echo "kill -9 1 at $(date)" is refused while echo "kill -9 1" passes, a false positive. The task:
• runs all 33 safety checks on three forms (plain double quotes, single quotes, quotes with $(date)) and posts the summary before any code changes;
• fixes the one shared cause in the text-scanning pass. My guess is quote stripping, but that's unverified.
• requires some commands to stay refused: $(rm -rf /) inside quotes, bash -c/eval bodies, and every existing quoted and glued test;
• compares old and new verdicts over the whole test set and lists every change in both directions;
• includes the same sabotage check.

If any check still behaves differently after the fix, the task's title drops to "Part of #1196" instead of closing it.

